<id/19/1914/#concept> a <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E55_Type>, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Olibanum"@en ;
    skos:broader <id/grp/grp_gums_resins_naval_stores/#concept> ;
    skos:definition "a stimulating gum-resin, obtained in India from *Roswellia thurifera*, used medicinally and as a perfume. *See FRANKINCENSE*. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 277]"@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Curated classification (group=grp_gums_resins_naval_stores): Named gum-resin under an archaic spelling (olibanum; 'Benjamin' = benzoin, Simmonds 1892 s.v. BENJAMIN; 'camphire' = camphor) left in the residual bin. Layer-1 observations: 3 rows, 1866–1866. Series: HCPP_Annual Statement of Trade ×3. Units: CWTS (Hundredweights) ×3. Top routes: World → United Kingdom ×1; Other Parts → United Kingdom ×1; Bombay and Scinde → United Kingdom ×1."@en ;
